WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.427
This call copies the zero in CPU memory

00:00:03.427 --> 00:00:05.257
into a separate GPU array.

00:00:06.757 --> 00:00:09.355
CUDA loads the compiled kernel onto the

00:00:09.355 --> 00:00:10.469
GPU when needed.

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:15.120
One GPU thread runs the kernel using the

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.089
array already in GPU memory.

00:00:18.589 --> 00:00:21.016
Both arrays contain zero. Which array will

00:00:21.016 --> 00:00:22.749
change when this line runs?

00:00:26.249 --> 00:00:29.794
The GPU thread writes 42 to the GPU array.

00:00:29.794 --> 00:00:32.158
The CPU array still holds zero.

00:00:33.658 --> 00:00:36.261
Copy to host waits for the kernel to

00:00:36.261 --> 00:00:39.189
finish. It returns the value in a new CPU

00:00:39.189 --> 00:00:40.165
array called result.
